<opsproc code="00012799.0001001" revdate="2010-09-17T10:36:24"><title><tech-label type="pb">Rudder PEDALS DISC</tech-label></title><procdesc code="00012799.0001001.001" lid="N.00012799.0001001.002"><para code="00012799.0001001.002" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.003">The purpose of the procedure
is to explain how to perform the flight control check with one or
both <tech-label type="pb">PEDALS DISC</tech-label> failed in the released position.</para></procdesc><procitem layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.001"><title>General information</title><procbody lid="N.00012799.0001001.004"><ex-conditions lid="N.00012799.0001001.005"><condition at-any-time="false" code="00012799.0001001.003" direct="false" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.006" subtitle="false" type="cond"><intro>When the disconnection is not possible on one side:</intro><procbody lid="N.00012799.0001001.007"><inform layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.008"><para code="00012799.0001001.004" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.009">The flight control check can be performed on the operative side.</para></inform></procbody></condition><condition at-any-time="false" code="00012799.0001001.005" direct="false" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.010" subtitle="false" type="cond"><intro>When the disconnection is not possible on both sides:</intro><procbody lid="N.00012799.0001001.011"><inform layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.012"><para code="00012799.0001001.006" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.013">The flight control check must be performed while aircraft
is stopped.</para></inform><inform layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.014"><noteproc code="00012799.0001001.007" layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.015"><para layer="1" lid="N.00012799.0001001.016">it is not necessary to set the <tech-label type="sw">A/SKID &amp; N/W STRG</tech-label> to OFF.</para></noteproc></inform></procbody></condition></ex-conditions></procbody></procitem></opsproc>